frontends/nss: restart the stats sync when a reply goes missing

The CONN_STATS_SYNC_MANY chain is driven only by the reply callback,
which queues the next request. A lost reply stops the stats sync for
that family until ECM is reloaded, and conntrack then expires
accelerated connections the firmware still forwards.

Tag each request with a sequence number in app_data, which the firmware
echoes, and arm a 5 s timeout after sending it. On timeout, count it in
stats_request_counter, warn and restart the walk from index 0. A late
reply still has its records applied but does not queue another request.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Manuel Fombuena <fombuena@outlook.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

